# Fleeting Reflection on Bot1's tapped attacking Memnite (1/1) and Bot2's Ornithopter (0/2 flyer): the Memnite gains hexproof, untaps,
# and becomes a copy of the Ornithopter until end of turn (CR 707.2), so it is still attacking but deals no damage as a 0/2 flyer. It
# is the same object, so it does not enter again. On Bot2's turn it is a 1/1 Memnite again with no hexproof.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Memnite
Island
Mox Jet
Fleeting Reflection
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fleeting Reflection.Cast
Bot1.Target(Memnite)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying; Hexproof
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Power = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Toughness = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Keywords = (absent)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Fleeting Reflection
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
